# Store one line ending in the repository, whatever each machine uses on disk.
#
# Why this is here: if our two machines have different git line-ending settings,
# an editor that re-saves a file makes the whole file look rewritten. The real
# change is then buried in a diff of every line. This one rule prevents that,
# and it does not depend on either of us configuring anything locally.
#
# Nothing else belongs in this file. Git already detects .xlsx, .pdf, images and
# other binary formats by itself and refuses to merge them.

* text=auto
